31,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,Wow! I found out that picking a desk and plugging in takes almost ten minutes! And some people get here way before others!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The costs are rigid. We are billed by area, not people, and re-running power for every change is quite expensive per desk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It's worse than I thought. Daylight is a huge complaint, and unplanned shuffles in the past have caused weeks of interruptions.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"As I suspected. The noise by the printer is much higher, and the physio says it takes days to get a workstation setting right.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found something great! Sitting together helps people answer questions faster and helps new joiners learn the unwritten rules!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if it costs money to move, maybe we should just pick one spot and stay? But ten minutes every morning sounds like a lot!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, exactly. Frequent changes are a financial drain. We need a solution that minimizes the need to re-run power and network cables.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, if it takes days to settle a chair, then moving around constantly would be a nightmare for everyone's health.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, precisely. A system that forces us to reset our ergonomics every few days is logically unsound and physically draining.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But if we stay in one spot, will we stop talking to each other? The data shows that being close is how we actually learn!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, maybe we can just have a party at the desks! But I don't want to spend my whole morning plugging in cables.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,We must balance the social benefit Yumi mentioned with the reality of the budget and the installation costs.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"We also can't ignore the daylight issue. If we have fixed spots, we have to decide who gets the window fairly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"The noise levels are a major factor. Some of us need quiet to focus, and the printer area is a dead zone for productivity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, maybe we can rotate who gets the window? That way everyone gets some sun and we still stay close!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just want it to be easy! No more long plugging-in times and no more waiting for the late people to arrive!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Stability seems to be the common thread here, both for the budget and for the physical setup.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. We need a plan that avoids the chaos of unplanned shuffles and addresses the inequality of the desk locations.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,Any plan that ignores the time it takes to adjust a workstation is a failure. We need consistency.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"As long as we don't lose that magic of overhearing things and helping each other, I'm happy!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Okay! We have Option A, B, and C! A is no seats, B is rotating, and C is fixed by function. I don't like A!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is a waste of time every morning and Option B is a financial disaster due to the power re-running costs.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Option A would be unfair because the early birds always get the window seats. Option C is the most stable.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A and B are impossible. You cannot spend days adjusting a chair only to move it. Option C is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option C sounds a bit stiff, but if we group by function, we'll still be sitting with the people we need to talk to!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, you're right! If we're grouped by work, we can still be besties! I vote for Option C!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,Option C minimizes the cost of facilities and provides the budget stability we need. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"It allows us to explicitly assign the window seats and avoid the ""first-come"" unfairness of Option A. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,It is the only option that respects the physical requirements of the body and the need for a quiet environment. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"I was worried about the ""fixed"" part, but the benefit of learning from each other is still there in Option C. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! We all agree! No more plugging in for ten minutes every single day!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,It is a rational conclusion. We save money and reduce administrative friction.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,And we can finally settle the daylight dispute once and for all with a fair plan.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"Finally, a decision based on data rather than whim.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm just glad we're all on the same page! This is going to be a great new layout!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
